  "finalMessage": "Files already in place: `EddFromScanTest.kt`, `PatientDatingDraftTest.kt`, and the updated `IntakeDatingRuleTest.kt`. I did not edit anything; I read them against the spec and the production signatures. Nothing has been compiled or run (see below).\n\n**Check script**\n- I ran `check_r4g.py`. All six checks (S170–S175) fail on today's code, as intended.\n- The script and the `STATIC-r4g` and `UNIT-r4g` manifest entries look correct, so I left them alone.\n\n**Unit tests**\n- **Q270, `EddFromScanTest`:**\n  - 2026-03-01 at 8w3d gives 2026-10-08, and at 12w0d gives 2026-09-13.\n  - Invalid inputs return null: gaDays 7, gaDays -1, weeks -1 and weeks 43.\n  - Weeks 0 and 42 are accepted.\n- **Q271 and Q272, `PatientDatingDraftTest`:**\n  - The reducer sets each of the seven new fields, and changes only the named field.\n  - The seven fields default to blank.\n  - A draft saved with `draftRecordFor` and restored with `applyDraftRecord` keeps all seven values.\n  - An old record without the seven keys restores the current values unchanged.\n- **Q273, `IntakeDatingRuleTest`:**\n  - It uses the new `intakeDatingUpdate(existing, PatientDraftValues(...))` signature and keeps every earlier case and expectation.\n  - It adds the LMP method and note, blank method equal to LMP, and existing-patient with a non-LMP method returning null.\n  - It adds IVF, scan and Clinical cases with the spec's numbers. IVF and scan each have their bad-input cases returning null. Clinical covers a bad or blank date.\n  - It adds `intakeDatingPreview` tests.\n\n**Assumption on the preview GA**\n- The spec says GA \"26w2d\" for LMP 2026-02-01 at asOf 2026-08-01, but that date pair is 181 days, which is 25 weeks 6 days.\n- The engine's format also has a space. The test therefore expects `\"25w 6d\"`, with a comment saying so. The orchestrator should confirm the spec figure.\n\n**Not verified**\n- The unit tests will not compile until the core lane adds `eddFromScan`, the new `PatientDraftValues` fields and `PatientDraftField` entries, `IntakeDating`, `intakeDatingPreview` and the DraftMapping keys.\n- I did not run any of them. The helper names (`draftRecordFor`, `applyDraftRecord`, `DraftRecord.fields`, `PatientDraft`, `AncEvent.PatientDraftChanged`) are checked against current sources only.",
